# Overview

[nextjs supabase payments safety protocol — mandatory]

This rule applies to changes involving:
- next.js app router (app/)
- route handlers (app/api/**/route.ts)
- server actions
- supabase (auth, rls, queries)
- payments (stripe, toss, webhooks)
- secrets/env (api keys, webhook secrets)
- workspace switching and entitlements

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
1. app router correctness (critical)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
- Respect server/client boundaries:
  - "use client" only when needed.
  - Never import server-only modules into client components.
- Prefer server-side data fetching for sensitive data.
- Avoid leaking secrets into the client bundle.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2. env & secret handling (critical)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
- Never print, log, or expose secrets:
  - api keys
  - webhook secrets
  - tokens
  - supabase service role key
- Never put secrets into NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables.
- Do not add verbose request logging in webhook routes.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
3. webhook security baseline (critical)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
For webhook endpoints:
- Always verify signature (stripe/toss).
- Always make handler idempotent:
  - store event_id
  - ignore duplicates
- Never rely on request order.
- Return 200 quickly after safe persistence.
- No external network calls before verification.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
4. payment lifecycle invariants (critical)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
- checkout success must be confirmed by webhook, not by redirect page.
- redirects only show status; they do not create entitlements.
- entitlements/subscriptions must only be activated via verified webhook.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
5. supabase client separation (critical)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
- Browser client:
  - only for user-level operations.
  - never use service role key.
- Server client:
  - can use service role (if needed) but must be isolated to server code.
- All privileged DB writes must occur on the server.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
6. workspace and entitlement gating
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
- Every workspace page must:
  - resolve active workspace
  - load entitlements
  - gate UI and actions consistently
- Never silently fallback to "allow" if entitlement lookup fails.
- If entitlement cannot be confirmed → show safe degraded UI (read-only or paywall).

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
7. kr/en dual update (mandatory)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
If KR and EN pages/components exist for the same feature:
- Always apply equivalent changes to both.
- Keep logic identical; text only differs.
- Do not ship asymmetrical behavior.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
8. routing and path safety
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
- Avoid open redirects:
  - "next" params must be path-only and validated.
- Keep marketing vs workspace layout rules intact:
  - (marketing) has public header
  - (workspace) uses workspace header only

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
9. data fetching reliability
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
- Use explicit loading/error states.
- Avoid infinite spinners:
  - add timeouts or bounded retries where appropriate.
- Never swallow exceptions in auth/workspace resolution.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
10. logging policy (prod safe)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
- No sensitive logging.
- In dev, logs must be behind a __DEV__ guard.
- Webhook logs must never include payload bodies or headers in full.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
11. execution & verification steps (mandatory)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
After changes:
- run: lint
- run: typecheck (if configured)
- run: build
- fix minimal issues only, then re-run build
No refactoring during fix passes.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
12. hard stop conditions
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
STOP and ask before proceeding if:
- a change requires modifying more than 5 files
- a change affects webhook handlers + billing + rls at once
- schema cannot be verified via information_schema
- any secret handling is unclear

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
13. completion criteria
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
- build passes
- no type errors
- webhook verified + idempotent
- no secret exposure
- kr/en parity maintained

